VCI Lytx Vehicle Synchronization

Important File-Path Note

Windows user folders depend on the person running the automation. Any path containing C:\Users\jd0855\ must be changed to the current user's Windows profile path, such as C:\Users\<username>\.

Purpose

This project downloads the complete authorized vehicle report from the Lytx Admin Vehicles portal, validates the downloaded CSV, copies the required vehicle fields into the governed Google Sheet as values only, and saves the dated CSV in the designated report folder.

Source

Lytx portal:

https://dc.lytx.com/

Admin Vehicles page:

https://app.lytx.com/#/admin/vehicles

The automation uses the Download CSV control at the bottom of the Vehicle Management page and includes every downloaded vehicle.

Google Sheet Destination

Google Sheet ID:

1ZcpnQn6ZqXFhqaEShqMrWGIpEWKtH-Z-0z9ZGw-OXdw

Worksheet tab:

OOS Vehicles

Existing values in the governed destination columns are cleared from row 2 downward and replaced with the current Lytx vehicle data. Header row 1 is preserved.

Column Mapping

Lytx CSV column

Google Sheet column

Vehicle

Truck #

Group

Division - Data

Status

Status - Data

Only values are pasted. Existing destination formatting and unrelated columns are preserved.

CSV Destination

C:\Users\jd0855\Downloads\Reports\Lytx

The Windows username portion of this path depends on the current user.

Expected filename format:

YYYY-MM-DD_Vehicles_Lytx.csv

Example:

2026-09-04_Vehicles_Lytx.csv

Normal Use

Confirm the computer is connected to the internet.

Close any unnecessary automation Chrome windows.

Double-click run_lytx_vehicle_sync.bat.

If Lytx requests authentication, complete sign-in and MFA.

If prompted, manually open the Lytx Admin Vehicles page and wait until the vehicle list is fully visible.

Return to the terminal and press Enter when instructed.

If Google requests authentication, sign in with the authorized VCI Google account.

Confirm that the OOS Vehicles worksheet is visible and editable, then return to the terminal and press Enter.

Wait for the successful completion message.

Review the latest log if an error occurs.

Do not close the automation Chrome window while a download, Google Sheet update, or save operation is in progress.

First-Time Login Setup

Lytx Login

From Command Prompt in the project folder, run:

run_lytx_vehicle_sync.bat --setup-lytx

Sign in with the authorized VCI Lytx account, complete MFA if requested, navigate to the Admin Vehicles page, and press Enter in the terminal only after the vehicle list is visible.

Google Login

Run:

run_lytx_vehicle_sync.bat --setup-google

Sign in with the authorized VCI Google account and confirm that the OOS Vehicles worksheet is visible and editable. Press Enter in the terminal only after the worksheet is ready.

Configure Both Login Profiles

Run:

run_lytx_vehicle_sync.bat --setup-lytx --setup-google

The automation also detects an expired Google session during a normal run. If Google returns an authorization error, Chrome opens the destination spreadsheet and the script pauses so the user can sign in before it retries.

Browser Profiles

The project uses dedicated local Chrome profile folders for Lytx and Google authentication. These profiles retain the authorized sessions used by the automation.

Do not copy, share, email, or commit browser-profile folders. Each user must create their own local authenticated profiles.

Download and Validation Rules

The automation:

Reuses an existing Lytx Admin Vehicles tab when available.

Opens the configured vehicle page when it is not already open.

Scrolls the page until the Download CSV control renders.

Reads the vehicle count shown by Lytx.

Confirms that clicking the control actually creates a current-run download.

Retries the download control safely if no file starts.

Accepts only the expected dated Lytx vehicle filename.

Validates the required CSV headers.

Confirms that the CSV contains vehicle rows.

Updates Google Sheets only after the CSV passes validation.

Google Sheet Update Rules

The automation:

Opens or reuses the configured destination spreadsheet.

Detects and pauses for Google authentication when required.

Confirms the required destination headers exist.

Clears only the governed destination columns from row 2 downward.

Pastes Truck #, Division - Data, and Status - Data as values only.

Preserves row 1, unrelated columns, and existing worksheet formatting.

Verifies the completed update before reporting success.

Safety Controls

The Google Sheet is not intentionally changed unless the downloaded report:

Uses the expected filename format

Contains the required source headers

Contains populated vehicle rows

Passes CSV processing and validation

The final dated CSV is saved only after the Google Sheet update succeeds. A failed run writes details to the log and reports that the existing destination data was not intentionally changed after the failure.

Logs

Run logs are saved in:

logs

Diagnostic screenshots may also be saved in this folder when the Lytx download step fails.

Troubleshooting

Lytx login expired

Run:

run_lytx_vehicle_sync.bat --setup-lytx

Complete Lytx sign-in and MFA, then confirm the Admin Vehicles page is visible.

Google returned HTTP 401

During a normal run, follow the Google authentication prompt in Chrome and press Enter after the OOS Vehicles worksheet is visible and editable.

You can also refresh the login profile manually:

run_lytx_vehicle_sync.bat --setup-google

Download control not found

Confirm that Chrome displays the Lytx Vehicle Management page and that the vehicle list has finished loading. The Download CSV control is located at the bottom of the page.

Download did not start

Keep the automation Chrome window open. The script retries the download control automatically. If all attempts fail, refresh the Lytx login profile and rerun the automation.

Partial .crdownload file

A .crdownload file means Chrome started but did not finalize the download. Do not manually rename an incomplete file. Review the latest log and rerun after confirming the Lytx page is fully loaded.

Google Sheet tab closed

The updater keeps a separate browser tab alive and recreates the destination spreadsheet tab when needed. Do not manually close the entire automation Chrome window while the update is running.

Required header missing

Confirm the Lytx CSV includes:

Vehicle

Group

Status

Confirm the OOS Vehicles worksheet includes:

Truck #

Division - Data

Status - Data

Python virtual environment not found

Complete the first-time project setup and confirm this file exists:

.venv\Scripts\python.exe

Code compilation check

Run:

.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m py_compile src\main.py src\lytx_download.py src\google_sheet_update.py src\csv_processor.py

No output means the Python files passed the structural code check.